    "narrative": "Today\u2019s optimal lineup for the Austin Waves is headlined by **Gunnar Henderson** (63.77) and **Heliot Ramos** (61.69). **Gunnar Henderson** is our premier play, as the matchup against Ryan Weathers offers significant stolen base upside; the combination of a favorable hitter\u2019s park and a slow delivery from the opposing pitcher bolsters his efficiency score well into the \"Strong\" tier despite a platoon disadvantage. Similarly, **Heliot Ramos** benefits from a massive 19% boost in his projection due to an advantageous matchup against Roki Sasaki (xERA 5.30), providing us with high-ceiling production despite the inherent risk of facing a high-octane arm.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench involved **Josh Jung**, whose score of 46.79 narrowly missed the cut for the starting rotation. While **Josh Jung** is a viable asset, his matchup against Michael Soroka was dampened by a negative SP skill adjustment, leading the optimizer to prioritize the slightly higher-scoring **Nolan Schanuel** (47.75) and the strategic slotting of **Josh Lowe** (41.11). Elsewhere, we remain cautious regarding the top of our lineup; **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (55.86) and **Kyle Tucker** (53.64) are facing elite arms in Drew Rasmussen and Trevor McDonald, respectively. While these players are daily locks, their efficiency is depressed today by tough SP skill ratings and neutral-to-negative platoon environments.\n\nMonitor the status of our \"Lineup Pending\" designations closely, as any deviation in the batting order for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** or **Andy Pages**\u2014currently slotted at #3\u2014will force an immediate reassessment of their run production potential. **Andy Pages** (46.31) specifically faces pressure from a 1.86s pop-time catcher, adding a layer of risk to his base-running profile. We are currently navigating the absences of **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg** on the IL, further thinning our bench depth, so maintain vigilance for any last-minute weather or injury announcements that could disrupt the projected starting nine.",
